{
    "background_story": "Uriel was a charismatic actor in 19th-century Europe, renowned for his comedic timing and impressive physical agility. His claim to fame was playing the lead role in a popular pantomime troupe, where he would don a colorful pantaloon costume and entertain audiences with his acrobatic antics. Uriel's performances were a masterclass in slapstick humor, with his oversized pantaloons getting tangled in the most ridiculous and hilarious ways. Offstage, Uriel was a kind and gentle soul, beloved by his fellow performers and the theater crew. Despite the physical demands of his role, he continued to delight audiences well into his later years, earning the nickname 'The Pantaloon King' among fans and critics alike. Uriel's legacy as a master of comedic pantomime lived on long after he took his final bow.",
